[2026-11-26T20:38:52.810Z] [INFO]       "output": "Native Codex runtime omits codex-code-mode-host, so Codex tasks cannot execute tools\n\n## Summary\n\nCodex tasks start and can talk to the model, but every tool attempt fails because the pinned native Codex runtime omits `codex-code-mode-host`. The binary exists in the upstream `@openai/codex-linux-x64` vendor package, but the Hive Mind native-codex installer copies only `codex` and the manifest/recipe/license files. Codex then fails closed:\n\n```text\nCode Mode is unavailable because failed to spawn code-mode host\n/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@openai/.hive-native-codex-9nGHu0/codex-code-mode-host:\nhost executable was not found. Code mode will fail closed; enable\n`features.code_mode_host` and install `codex-code-mode-host`.\n```\n\nThe model still produces a final “blocked by environment” message, so the task looks like it ran but did no work.\n\n## Environment\n\n- Hive Mind `2.50.0`\n- Task image `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.50.0`\n- DooD deployment; Docker socket mounted\n- Native Codex `0.164.0`\n- `codex features list` reports `code_mode_host  stable  true`\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Start a Codex task with Docker isolation, e.g. `/codex --think xhigh`.\n2. The task reaches Codex and emits `thread.started`.\n3. On the first tool attempt:\n\n```text\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"Code Mode is unavailable because failed to spawn code-mode host /home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@openai/.hive-native-codex-9nGHu0/codex-code-mode-host: host executable was not found. Code mode will fail closed; enable `features.code_mode_host` and install `codex-code-mode-host`.\"}}\n```\n\n```text\nERROR session_loop{...}: codex_core::tools::router: error=failed to spawn code-mode host\n/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@openai/.hive-native-codex-9nGHu0/codex-code-mode-host:\nNo such file or directory (os error 2)\n```\n\nThe task then reports `codex-code-mode-host is missing` and exits without changes. Example: PR #17 on `link-foundation/universal-translator`, comment 7202114824.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/native-codex-runtime.lib.mjs` builds the admitted file set as:\n\n```js\nconst files = new Set(['codex', 'manifest.json', 'source.json', 'recipe.json']);\n```\n\nand then adds license files. The installed generation `.hive-native-codex-*` contains only those files. The native Codex binary resolves its code-mode host next to its own executable, so it looks for:\n\n```text\n.../.hive-native-codex-<suffix>/codex-code-mode-host\n```\n\nThat file is absent. The upstream npm vendor package already ships it:\n\n```text\n/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex-code-mode-host\n```\n\nIt is 76,997,904 bytes and reports the same `codex-cli 0.164.0` version. The native-codex build/publish pipeline and the installer both omit it, and `verify()` would currently reject it as an unexpected file if it were added manually.\n\n## Workaround that works\n\nBuild a patched task image that:\n\n1. Copies `codex-code-mode-host` from the upstream vendor package into:\n   - the native variant runtime:\n     `/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@link-assistant/hive-mind-native-codex-linux-x64/runtime/linux-x64/`\n   - the installed generation:\n     `/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@openai/.hive-native-codex-*/`\n2. Adds `codex-code-mode-host` to the admitted `files` set in `src/native-codex-runtime.lib.mjs` so `verify()` accepts it.\n3. Retags the patched image as `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.50.0` (and `:latest`) on the host.\n\nDockerfile used:\n\n```dockerfile\nFROM konard/hive-mind-dind:2.50.0\nUSER root\nRUN set -eux; \\\n    host=/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex-code-mode-host; \\\n    variant=/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@link-assistant/hive-mind-native-codex-linux-x64/runtime/linux-x64; \\\n    for d in \"$variant\" /home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@openai/.hive-native-codex-*; do \\\n      [ -d \"$d\" ] || continue; \\\n      cp -f \"$host\" \"$d/codex-code-mode-host\"; \\\n      chown box:box \"$d/codex-code-mode-host\"; \\\n      chmod 755 \"$d/codex-code-mode-host\"; \\\n    done; \\\n    f=/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@link-assistant/hive-mind/src/native-codex-runtime.lib.mjs; \\\n    sed -i \"s/const files = new Set(\\['codex', 'manifest.json'/const files = new Set(['codex', 'codex-code-mode-host', 'manifest.json'/\" \"$f\"; \\\n    grep -q \"'codex-code-mode-host'\" \"$f\"\nUSER box\n```\n\nVerified:\n\n- `verifyNativeCodexCommand()` returns the native entrypoint successfully.\n- A real `codex exec` in the patched image, with the same flags Hive Mind uses, now runs commands:\n\n```text\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'printf codex-host-ok'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"codex-host-ok\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n```\n\nThe test used `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`, matching the actual task command.\n\n## Suggested fixes\n\n1. **Build/publish fix:** include `codex-code-mode-host` in the native-codex variant artifact, manifest, and `files` set, and verify its bytes/hash like `codex`.\n2. **Installer fix:** copy the host binary from the variant runtime into the installed generation; keep the existing exclusive-publication checks.\n3. **Verification fix:** admit `codex-code-mode-host` in `verify()` and reject it if missing, so a broken generation fails early with a clear message instead of failing on the first tool call.\n4. **Regression test:** assert that the installed generation contains both `codex` and `codex-code-mode-host`, and that a trivial `codex exec` tool call succeeds.\n5. **Fallback:** if the host binary cannot be shipped for a platform, disable `features.code_mode_host` by default for that platform so Codex uses the normal tool path instead of failing closed.\n\n## Related\n\n- #4157 — DooD `.gitconfig` mount backing failure (the previous blocker on the same host)\n- PR link-foundation/universal-translator#17 — task that exposed this\n- The task log warns this as “non-fatal” and treats the turn as completed (see #1955), which hides the fact that no tools ran. Consider escalating `Code Mode is unavailable` to a failed session when code mode is required.\n\n## Impact\n\nAll Codex tasks on this deployment start, consume tokens, and then fail before any tool executes. Claude tasks are unaffected.\n\n\n__formal_ai_exit=0\n",
